# interplay_lifetime_icb_writeback_after_delete: What an ICB's write-back (53, isolate only: in-process it aborts, docs/testing.md section 7.4) says about objects deleted and made again since it was prepared. The service resolves a command's bind from its GPU address through the addresses buffers registered at creation, and a pipeline from its unique identifier through the pipelines registered at creation; deletes never unregister. A bound buffer deleted (37) is not found ("Resource not found for GPU address": the bind is written as reference ~0, offset 0); made again by an exec, the old address finds the old entry, whose reference names the new buffer, so the bind is written as before. A deleted pipeline (40, operation 1006) is still named by its reference. A second pipeline built from an identical record (over a function of its own) registers whatever unique identifier Metal gives it; on this host Metal gives it a new one, so the ICB's command still names the first reference. Only references and offsets are dumped; keyed by the host because Metal's pipeline identity is the host's.
